From: Proton CRM <noreply@proton.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Contact views: mask phone, e-mail and IC for users without
 pii.view (Wave 2 Task 29, FIX-49)

RFP 2026_028 2.2.5 asks to "validate data masking (PII protection)"; PDPA
2010. The backend masks its own responses (Customer 360, RSA, case fields,
AI activity) when PII_MASKING_ENABLED is on. Chatwoot's own contact views are
not backend responses, so this patch masks them on the client:

* useProtonPiiMask.js (new): asks GET /authz/me/pii once per page session
  (under /authz/*, already routed to the backend by every tenant vhost).
  Fail closed: masked while the answer is pending and on an error (retried
  after 5 s); unmasked on a 404 (older backend / route absent) or when no
  Proton backend is configured, and on any answer other than
  { masking_enabled: true, masked: true }. Same display format as the
  backend (+60•••••6789, s•••@gmail.com, ******-**-5678) and the same
  anchored key rules (ic/nric/mykad, passport, vin/chassis, bank account /
  account / card number, phone, e-mail; bank_name is not masked).
* ContactInfo.vue (conversation contact sidebar): e-mail, phone and
  identifier rows masked; masked rows are not copyable, not editable and
  carry no mailto:/tel: link; the edit-contact modal button is hidden.
  The call button still works (the agent can call without seeing).
* ContactsCard.vue (contact list): e-mail and phone masked; the inline edit
  form, which shows the full values, is not offered.
* CustomAttributes.vue (sidebar contact/conversation attributes): an
  attribute whose key names personal data is shown masked and read-only, and
  a masked value is never saved back.

UX only: Chatwoot's API still returns raw values to the browser. Not covered
(Wave 3): the contact details page, message bodies, search results, the
contacts CSV export, and Chatwoot's own API.

